{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01XLZ6zKvcMxakv9kTiq3Kew","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Q48 written, validate passed, category complete.**\n\nAnswer note `01-048-imbalanced-datasets-how-handle.md` covers:\n\n- **Three-layer mitigation playbook** in the right order: (1) fix metrics first — PR-AUC over accuracy, because ROC-AUC is inflated by the majority class; (2) algorithm-level — `class_weight='balanced'`/`pos_weight` in PyTorch or focal loss, both free; (3) data-level — SMOTE for tabular, LLM-based paraphrase augmentation for text (SMOTE on embeddings produces incoherent points)\n- **Threshold tuning** — calibrate with Platt/temperature scaling, then pick the operating point on the PR curve that satisfies your business SLO (e.g., recall ≥ 0.95 for fraud)\n- **Production angle** — imbalance ratios drift over time; monitor precision/recall separately on a rolling window, not just overall accuracy\n- **LLM fine-tuning edge case** — fewer than ~100 minority examples → few-shot prompting or RAG classification beats fine-tuning\n\nValidate: **ALL PASSED** (49/49 files) — category `01-llm-fundamentals` is fully complete.\n\n<promise>COMPLETE</promise>"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":61413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":311,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"933eaa9d-c4db-4f4b-8363-95323b7eeb64","uuid":"d2c5be00-35e1-4a5b-8835-574c57ed11be"}
